WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:35.500
My name is Robin, I'm from Switzerland and growing up in Switzerland, Robin was not a common name for girls and as a kid that was really hard because Robin was strictly seen as a boy's name and kids can be brutal as we all know so I was teased a lot in school and it really got to the point where I generally started to hate my own name and I was so determined to change it once I turned 18 and I was also angry at my parents for giving me a boy's name in the first place so yeah, it was quite a lot, but then something unexpected happened.
我叫罗宾（Robin），我来自瑞士。在瑞士长大时，罗宾对女孩来说并不是一个常见的名字，小时候这真的很难熬，因为罗宾严格意义上被视为一个男孩的名字，而且正如我们所知，小孩子可能会很残酷，所以我上学时经常被取笑，这真的到了我开始痛恨自己名字的地步，我甚至下定决心等我满18岁时一定要改名，而且我也很生父母的气，怪他们当初给我起了个男孩名，所以，是的，压力真的很大，但接着发生了一件意想不到的事。

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:43.820
Around 2010, how would your mother really blew up in Switzerland, or at least at my school, and everyone was watching it.
大约在2010年左右，《老爸老妈浪漫史》真的在瑞士大火特火，或者至少在我们学校是这样，每个人都在看。

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:50.780
Like, the cool kids were watching it, the people who wanted to be cool, and everyone knew the jokes and the references and everything.
就像，酷盖们在看，那些想装酷的人在看，每个人都知道里面的笑话、梗以及各种内容。

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.460
And yeah, suddenly my name wasn't something people laughed at anymore.
然后，是的，突然之间，我的名字不再是人们嘲笑的对象了。

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.497
It became cool.
它变酷了。

00:00:55.497 --> 00:00:57.020
It became really cool.
它变得真的很酷。

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:07.744
And for the first time in my life, I almost felt like people people were jealous that I had this cool international name that was the same name as one of the characters on the show.
而且我这辈子头一次，甚至觉得人们开始嫉妒我拥有这个酷炫的国际化名字，这个名字和剧中的一个角色一模一样。

00:01:07.744 --> 00:01:22.379
And yeah, when I then started watching the show myself, it was such a healing experience for me because not only did I see my name represented on screen, it was the name of the woman I personally thought was like the coolest character on the show.
所以，是的，当我后来自己开始看这部剧时，这对我来说是一次极其治愈的经历，因为我不仅在屏幕上看到了我的名字，而且它还是我个人认为剧中“最酷”的那个女主角的名字。

00:01:22.379 --> 00:01:32.689
And so yeah, I will always be grateful to how I met your mother and especially Robin Shabatski for helping me turn something I once hated something I know I'm truly proud of.
所以，是的，我将永远感激《老爸老妈浪漫史》，尤其是罗宾·什巴斯基（Robin Scherbatsky），感谢她帮我把一个曾经我讨厌的名字，变成了我真正引以为傲的名字。

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:33.459
So thank you.
所以谢谢你们。

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:53.870
I'm alone, won't be soon, you know what I see, permit me to tell you everything city.
我孤身一人，但不会太久，你知道我看到了什么，请允许我向你诉说这座城市的一切。

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:58.471
Well, Craig, what a great letter to start with.
好了，克雷格（Craig），多么棒的一封开场信啊。

00:01:58.471 --> 00:02:02.290
Are you like weirdly moved by that one?
你是不是对这个感到莫名的感动？

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.569
Oh, I found it so moving for somebody.
哦，我觉得这太让人感动了，对某个人来说。

00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:12.430
Yeah, out of all the things you think you're doing when you're making a TV show, and we We thought we were doing some things.
是的，在你拍电视剧的时候，你想着自己能成就各种各样的事，而我们也确实觉得自己做成了一些事。

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:13.430
Right.
没错。

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:21.849
We were not thinking that we were helping a teenage girl in Switzerland adjust to and love her name.
我们可没想过我们是在帮瑞士的一个十几岁女孩适应并爱上她的名字。

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:24.810
We were not thinking that.
我们根本没想过这个。

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.729
That was outside the top 10 things we thought we were doing.
这甚至排不进我们自认为在做的事的前十名。

00:02:27.729 --> 00:02:29.090
It was just, it was number 11.
它只是，排在第11位。

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.490
It was almost in the top 10.
差不多进前十了。

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:31.490
Yeah.
对。

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:32.689
That's extraordinary.
这太非凡了。

00:02:32.689 --> 00:02:33.569
Thank you for that.
谢谢你分享这个。

00:02:33.569 --> 00:02:36.409
That's, I'm so, I just blows my mind.
这，我太，这简直让我惊呆了。

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:38.689
It blows my mind because your name is a big deal.
这真的让我大受震撼，因为名字是一件大事。

00:02:38.689 --> 00:02:41.150
what you feel about your name is a big deal.
你对你名字的感受是一件大事。

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:46.050
And the idea that this sort of arrived, the show arrives to her at the exact right moment.
而且这种感觉就像是，这部剧在恰到好处的时刻来到了她身边。

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:51.270
She needed a cool, a cool female robin showed up right when she needed it.
她需要一个酷酷的、女性的罗宾，而这个角色就在她最需要的时候出现了。

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.110
Right when she needed it.
就在她最需要的时候。

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:52.949
That's fantastic.
太棒了。

00:02:52.949 --> 00:02:53.789
She needed it and made it cool.
她需要它，然后剧集让它变得很酷。

00:02:53.789 --> 00:02:54.610
That's the best story.
这是最棒的故事。

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.789
I've never heard exactly that story about him in 28 years.
28年来，我从来没听过关于他的这样一个故事。

00:02:57.789 --> 00:03:04.430
You know, it does feel, if you get a kind of strange name as a kid, it's hard, but as an adult, it's cool.
你知道的，如果你小时候有一个奇奇怪怪的名字，那确实很难熬，但长大后，这其实挺酷的。

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:05.270
Right.
对吧。

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.270
You just have to weather those years, right?
你只需要熬过那些年，对吧？

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:08.590
You have to weather those years.
你必须熬过那些年。

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:14.349
Yeah, but there is something you're sent like, I didn't and sort of still don't like the name Craig.
对，但有些事你会觉得，我以前不喜欢、现在也还是有点不太喜欢“Craig”这个名字。

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:15.909
It's definitely hard always.
这总是挺难的。

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:18.669
So every moment of your life, somebody going, Greg?
所以你生命中的每一刻，都会有人问：“Greg（格雷格）？”

00:03:18.669 --> 00:03:21.949
No, I'm the B team version of that name.
不，我是那个名字的B队备选版。

00:03:21.949 --> 00:03:23.030
It's actually Craig.
其实是Craig（克雷格）。

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.090
Why do you think Craig is the B?
你为什么觉得Craig是B备选？

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:28.550
I just, because everybody says Greg and they have to go to now, Craig.
我就是觉得，因为每个人都说成Greg，然后他们不得不改口说，哦，Craig。

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.550
And I've met other Craig's and they're like, yeah, fuck.
而且我遇到过其他叫Craig的人，他们都说，对啊，真他妈的。

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:40.030
I was told, I was told by my friend, Zach, that guys named Zach get mistakenly called Josh all the time.
我朋友扎克（Zach）曾告诉我，叫扎克的人经常被误叫成乔什（Josh）。

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.909
And I thought this was so strange because they don't even sound like the same name.
我觉得这太奇怪了，因为它们听起来根本就不像同一个名字。

00:03:43.909 --> 00:03:44.984
They don't share letters.
它们连字母都不一样。

00:03:44.984 --> 00:03:45.629
I looked it up.
我查了一下。

00:03:45.629 --> 00:03:47.764
There's a huge Reddit thread about it.
Reddit上有一个关于这个的超长讨论串。

00:03:47.764 --> 00:03:50.629
Like any other zacks out there getting called Josh.
就像其他叫扎克的总被人叫成乔什一样。

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.466
Alec has a son named Zach.
亚历克有个儿子叫扎克。

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:55.349
You have to ask.
你得去问问。

00:03:55.909 --> 00:03:56.349
Yeah.
对。

00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:57.750
See, I'm right now.
你看，我现在就……

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.110
Is it ever happened to your son?
这种事在你儿子身上发生过吗？

00:04:00.189 --> 00:04:00.949
Oh, I will ask him.
哦，我会去问他的。

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:03.550
I, of course, get, I mean, as Alec.
我当然会，我是说，作为亚历克。

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.502
Alec and Alex.
亚历克和亚历克斯。

00:04:04.502 --> 00:04:05.455
It's the same.
是一样的。

00:04:05.455 --> 00:04:25.803
You are the Craig of out to Alex and Craig Greg and Alec out weirdest thing for me though I my name is Josh and people call me Ted that's so Welcome to how we made your mother we haven't even said that you have the opposite experience of our Swiss yeah, exactly Ted ruined your life I'm Josh Radner.
你对亚历克斯和克雷格来说就像……格雷格和亚历克对我来说最奇怪的事是，我叫乔什，但人们叫我泰德，太……欢迎收听《老爸老妈的浪漫史》幕后揭秘，我们刚才甚至都没说你有和我们截然相反的经历，对，没错，泰德毁了你的生活，我是乔什·拉德纳。

00:04:25.803 --> 00:04:32.473
I played Ted mosey on a TV show called how we met your mother, which ran on CBS from 2005 to 2014.
我在一部名为《老爸老妈的浪漫史》的电视剧中饰演泰德·莫斯比，该剧于2005年至2014年在CBS播出。

00:04:32.473 --> 00:04:37.849
I'm with my good friend Craig Thomas who co-created the show with Carter Bayes.
和我在一起的是我的好朋友克雷格·托马斯，他和卡特·贝恩斯共同创作了这部剧。

00:04:37.849 --> 00:04:38.530
Hi, Craig.
嗨，克雷格。

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.346
Greg Thomas.
格雷格·托马斯。

00:04:39.346 --> 00:04:40.163
Greg Thomas.
格雷格·托马斯。

00:04:40.163 --> 00:04:42.477
Wait, I'm sorry, I never got easy.
等等，抱歉，我从来没搞懂过。

00:04:42.477 --> 00:04:43.430
Greg or Craig.
格雷格还是克雷格。

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:46.152
You've been saying it wrong this whole time.
你一直以来都叫错名字了。

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.069
Craig Maylands and Greg Thomas.
克雷格·梅兰兹和格雷格·托马斯。

00:04:48.069 --> 00:04:49.478
Exactly.
没错。

00:04:49.478 --> 00:04:50.533
Craig.
克雷格。

00:04:50.533 --> 00:04:51.589
Craig.
克雷格。

00:04:51.589 --> 00:04:52.469
Okay.
好的。

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.674
We are barreling through season two.
我们正在全力推进第二季。

00:04:54.674 --> 00:04:56.021
Thanks for joining us.
感谢收听。

00:04:56.021 --> 00:05:02.390
We're having such a good time I'm going through these episodes, which we haven't seen for quite a while.
我们重温这些已经很久没看过的剧集时过得很开心。

00:05:02.389 --> 00:05:05.750
Today's episode is called Bachelor Party.
今天的这集叫“单身派对”。

