00:05:08.829 --> 00:05:14.629
I'm gonna tell you, but first of all, let's tell you that my son just texted me and said, yes, people do call me, Josh, why are you at?
我来告诉你，不过首先，我得告诉你我儿子刚刚给我发信息说，对，确实有人叫我乔什，你是在哪儿……

00:05:14.629 --> 00:05:16.870
Oh my God, so that's really a thing.
天呐，所以这真的是个现象。

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:20.829
That is actually, you've never talked to your son, Zack, about this, until this moment, all right?
事实上，在此之前你从来没跟你儿子扎克聊过这事，直到刚才这一刻？

00:05:20.829 --> 00:05:22.189
Never, never.
从来没有，从来没有。

00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:29.829
I wonder if it's like a little, it's a thing in our brain That's like a weird human dyslexic thing.
我在想这会不会是某种……我们大脑里一种奇怪的、人类认知失调似的小状况。

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:34.629
Like, I don't know what is going on with Josh and Zach, but maybe it's like- It's something there.
就像，我不知道乔什和扎克之间是怎么回事，但也许它……这里面有文章。

00:05:34.629 --> 00:05:35.129
Yeah.
对。

00:05:35.129 --> 00:05:36.382
It's one syllable.
